>Does anybody know anything about how rusting works in 3.1?

>In NH 3.0 a rusted weapon would simply lose one of its plusses, and you  
>could reverse this by simply reading a scroll enchant weapon.

>In NH 3.1, though, no plusses are lost when a weapon rusts and the words  
>"rusted," "very rusted," or completely rusted" (or mayby corroded, I'm not  
>sure) appear in the description.

>Can anybody tell me what real effects this has on the item's performance,  
>and if it's reversable and if so, how?

You sense the presence of spoilers--more--


Rustproofing the item will remove all the rust. And, until you get it
rustproofed, you can protect your weapons (and armor) from (further)
rusting by applying grease to them.

As for the first question, I'm not sure what effect rust has, but I know
(from experience) that there are at least three levels of rustiness.  I
presume that at some point (probably after four rustings) that the item
just falls to pieces.
